---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import ContentImage from '../components/ContentImage.astro'
import { NOW, nowMonth } from '../lib/site'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Tarlow is a solo developer in Portland, Oregon building local-first tools, automation, and AI software."
  view="about"
>
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="about">
      <header class="about-head">
        <div>
          <p class="label"><span class="label-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>About</p>
          <h1>A bit about <em>me.</em></h1>
          <p class="about-deck">
            Solo developer in Portland, Oregon. Building local-first tools, automations, and software people
            can actually use.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="about-portrait about-polaroid">
          <div class="portrait-orbit" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="portrait-frame">
            <ContentImage
              src="/images/grandma.png"
              alt="Tarlow as a young child with his grandmother, in an old Polaroid photograph"
              sizes="(max-width: 720px) 230px, 320px"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="portrait-cap">
            <span>Tarlow<br />Portland, OR</span>
            <span>Building again<br />with better focus</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="about-story">
        <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="chapter-build">
          <div class="chapter-side">
            <span class="chapter-num">01</span>
            <span class="chapter-name">The start</span>
          </div>
          <div class="chapter-copy">
            <h2 id="chapter-build">Building came first.</h2>
            <p>
              I have been tinkering with tech since I was a kid, modding consoles, then PCs, then websites.
              From there I got into internet marketing and web development, where I fell for automation:
              taking a repetitive, boring task and letting software handle it instead.
            </p>
            <p>
              In 2014 that turned into BoosterBots, a software company where I built Windows automation
              tools and custom software for paying customers. Designing, shipping, and supporting desktop
              apps taught me more about building real products than anything else I have done.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="chapter-break">
          <div class="chapter-side">
            <span class="chapter-num">02</span>
            <span class="chapter-name">The break</span>
          </div>
          <div class="chapter-copy">
            <h2 id="chapter-break">Why I stepped back.</h2>
            <p>
              The software worked, and people paid for it. The issue was that those tools fought the
              platforms they ran on, so anything could break overnight and I did not want to spend my life
              chasing rules or building software that could get shut down.
            </p>
            <p>
              Stepping back was uncomfortable at times, and it took a while to sort out what I actually
              wanted to build next.
            </p>
            <p class="chapter-quote">"I took a break from everything, not a vacation."</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="chapter-return">
          <div class="chapter-side">
            <span class="chapter-num">03</span>
            <span class="chapter-name">The return</span>
          </div>
          <div class="chapter-copy">
            <h2 id="chapter-return">Coming back to build again.</h2>
            <p>
              Around 2023 and 2024, AI models and coding tools got good enough to build real products on
              my own machine. I had been waiting for the tools to catch up to the ideas in my head, and
              suddenly they had.
            </p>
            <p>
              Shipping Handmade Checker reminded me how much I enjoy building things from scratch and putting
              something genuinely useful in front of people.
            </p>
            <p>
              That grew into Moss AI Studio, my one-person shop for practical local-first and AI tools. Same
              interest in automation, just focused on software I can stand behind. I wrote the full backstory
              over at
              <a href="https://mossaistudio.com/blog/the-story-behind-moss-ai-studio/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Moss AI Studio</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="chapter-work">
          <div class="chapter-side">
            <span class="chapter-num">04</span>
            <span class="chapter-name">The work</span>
          </div>
          <div class="chapter-copy">
            <h2 id="chapter-work">How I work now.</h2>
            <p>
              Today I build tools for everyday bottlenecks: Handmade Checker, IndieGameScout, Pixel Juice
              Studio, and Marimo Bot. Alongside my own releases, I take on custom builds and automation
              projects through the studio for people who are tired of doing repetitive work by hand.
            </p>
            <p>
              Moss grows slowly and sticks around, which is the pace I want for my work too. Outside of
              work, I am usually camping, fishing, or spending time out at the beach.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <section class="about-quote-band" aria-label="A line from the story">
        <blockquote>
          "I wanted to stop fighting platforms and start building software I can actually stand behind."
        </blockquote>
        <p class="quote-attrib">From BoosterBots to Moss AI Studio.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="practice" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
        <div class="practice-head">
          <div>
            <p class="label"><span class="label-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>How I keep it steady</p>
            <h2 id="practice-title">Three habits I try to keep.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Simple reminders so I don't burn out or chase too many repos at once.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="practice-grid">
          <div class="practice-item">
            <span class="practice-index">01 / Focus</span>
            <h3>Finish fewer things.</h3>
            <p>The small details only show up when you slow down enough to give a project a second pass.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="practice-item">
            <span class="practice-index">02 / Pace</span>
            <h3>Keep it sustainable.</h3>
            <p>Steady progress beats juggling six repos at once and leaving half of them unfinished.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="practice-item">
            <span class="practice-index">03 / Health</span>
            <h3>Step away from the desk.</h3>
            <p>Walking, getting outside, and time at the beach keep my head clear for the work.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-now" aria-labelledby="about-now-title">
        <div>
          <p class="label"><span class="label-line" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Now / <span data-now-month>{nowMonth()}</span></span></p>
          <h2 id="about-now-title">Where I am <em>now.</em></h2>
          <p class="now-sub">
            Same builder, same interest in automation, with a clearer filter on what is worth building.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="now-list">
          <li>
            <span class="now-key">Building</span>
            <span class="now-value">
              {NOW.building.map((item, index) => (
                <span class="now-building">
                  {index > 0 && <span class="now-sep" aria-hidden="true"> + </span>}
                  <a href={item.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{item.label}</a>
                </span>
              ))}
            </span>
          </li>
          <li><span class="now-key">Practicing</span><span class="now-value">{NOW.practicing}</span></li>
          <li><span class="now-key">At home</span><span class="now-value">{NOW.home}</span></li>
          <li><span class="now-key">Open to</span><span class="now-value">{NOW.openTo}</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="about-contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
        <h2 id="contact-title">Want to talk through a build or project? Reach out.</h2>
        <div class="contact-links">
          <a href="mailto:tarlow@mossaistudio.com">Email</a>
          <a href="https://mossaistudio.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Moss AI Studio ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/DevTarlow/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
          <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/mossaistudio.bsky.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluesky ↗</a>
          <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
